hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21034","Ismail narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif, he said: two hadiths reached me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I have known that I believed them both, I do not know which of them was before the other. Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, Jadhimah Abd al-Qays, narrated to us, al-Jarud narrated to us, he said: while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and riding animals were few, when the people discussed riding animals, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I know what suffices us of riding animals. He said: and what suffices us? I said: a herd we come upon in a ravine, and we enjoy their backs. He said: no, the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not come near it. The stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not come near it. The stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not come near it."
"21035","And he said about lost property: the stray you find, then announce it, and do not conceal it nor hide it. If it is recognized, then return it, otherwise it is the wealth of Allah which He gives to whom He wills."
"21036","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, and Ahmad al-Haddad said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Jarud al-Abdi, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire, so do not come near it."
"21037","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"21038","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud ibn Mualla al-Abdi, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about strays, and he said: the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"21039","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Ala, from Abu Muslim, from al-Jarud, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"21040","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: the stray of the Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
